@page "/agents/financial-crime"

<PageTitle>Financial Crime Agent — Wealth Team in a Day</PageTitle>

<div class="agent-header" style="--accent: #ef4444">
    <a class="back-link" href="/"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Back to the operations office</a>
    <div class="agent-header-row">
        <div class="agent-header-icon">🛡️</div>
        <div>
            <div class="agent-header-dept">Financial Crime</div>
            <h1>Financial Crime Agent</h1>
            <div class="agent-header-persona">Felix — Financial Crime Investigator</div>
            <p class="tagline">Protects members from fraud, scams and identity takeover.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="agent-tab-scope" style="--accent: #ef4444">
    <nav class="agent-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Financial Crime agent details">
        <button type="button" class="agent-tab active" data-tab="overview" role="tab" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0">Overview</button>
        <button type="button" class="agent-tab" data-tab="try" role="tab" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Try it out</button>
    </nav>

    <div class="agent-tab-panel active" data-panel="overview" role="tabpanel">
    <section class="panel" style="--accent: #ef4444">
        <h2>What this agent does</h2>
        <p>
            Felix's agent protects members' super and investments from fraud, scams and identity
            takeover, and supports Caldova's AML/CTF obligations. It checks documents for tampering,
            builds the account-activity timeline, tests rollovers to self-managed super funds against
            the ATO's verification results, screens new clients and claimants, and explains every risk
            indicator in plain English — so a human investigator can decide quickly and fairly.
        </p>
        <div class="two-col">
            <div>
                <h3>Responsibilities</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Check identity documents, bank statements, SMSF details, death certificates and hardship letters for authenticity.</li>
                    <li>Build the account-activity timeline — contact-detail changes, new devices, MFA events, money-out requests and travel notices.</li>
                    <li>Test rollovers to SMSFs against the ATO SMSF verification service (SVS) and known red flags.</li>
                    <li>Screen new clients and claimants (KYC, politically exposed persons and sanctions).</li>
                    <li>Produce an explainable risk score with the evidence behind every indicator.</li>
                    <li>Recommend proportionate controls — holds, account locks, call-backs on trusted numbers, IDCARE referral and SMR consideration.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h3>Tools available</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Azure Content Understanding — document authenticity (custom field schema + checks layer)</li>
                    <li>Account-activity timeline</li>
                    <li>ATO SMSF verification service (SVS) result reader</li>
                    <li>PEP and sanctions screening</li>
                    <li>AUSTRAC / ATO red-flag guide via Azure AI Search (<code>wealth_knowledge</code>)</li>
                    <li>Explainable risk scoring</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Human approval</h3>
                <p class="approval">
                    Always required before blocking or holding a request on financial-crime grounds,
                    locking an account or online access, lodging a suspicious matter report (SMR) with
                    AUSTRAC, or contacting a member about suspected fraud.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel" style="--accent: #ef4444">
        <h2>How Felix's agent works</h2>
        <div class="two-col">
            <div>
                <h3>Guardrails</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Never accuses.</strong> Neutral, evidence-based language — "indicator", "inconsistency", "needs verification". In an identity takeover the member is the victim.</li>
                    <li><strong>No tipping off.</strong> SMRs, and the suspicion behind them, stay confidential.</li>
                    <li><strong>Trusted contacts only.</strong> Call-backs use the details on file before any change — never details supplied with the request.</li>
                    <li><strong>Privacy first.</strong> TFNs and bank account numbers stay masked (for example <code>*** *** 418</code>, <code>****7781</code>).</li>
                    <li><strong>Proportionate.</strong> Most requests are low risk and continue without extra friction — bereaved families and members in hardship aren't asked for more than is needed.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h3>Red flags it looks for</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Contact or payment details changed shortly before a withdrawal or rollover.</li>
                    <li>A new SMSF set up to receive someone's benefits.</li>
                    <li>Altered or fake identity and hardship documents.</li>
                    <li>A hardship request followed by a rollover to an SMSF.</li>
                    <li>Illegal early-release promoters and pushy "free super health check" switching offers.</li>
                    <li>Elder financial abuse — impersonation, or pressure to roll over to an SMSF someone else controls.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Controls it recommends</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Call back on the verified number on file.</li>
                    <li>Hold money-out requests after a recent change of details.</li>
                    <li>Dual approval for new payees; pay only to nominated or linked accounts.</li>
                    <li>SVS and ESA checks before any rollover to an SMSF.</li>
                    <li>Step-up (SMS code) verification for payments and changes.</li>
                    <li>An SMR to AUSTRAC within 3 business days of forming a suspicion — a human decision.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel" style="--accent: #ef4444">
        <h2>How this agent helps with a case</h2>
        <div class="demo">
            <p>
                When a request arrives to roll Grace Williams's whole balance — $612,400 — into a
                nine-day-old SMSF, Felix's agent lines up the evidence in seconds: her mobile and email
                were changed by phone about 93 hours earlier, a new device logged in from Sydney while
                her travel notice says Italy, the one-time code went to the new number, the ATO's SMSF
                verification fails, the payee account is in a company's name and the licence image has
                been altered. It scores the risk at 92/100 and recommends holding the rollover, locking
                online access and calling Grace on the number Caldova already trusted.
            </p>
            <p>
                Felix and the Team Leader make the call, and Grace's money never leaves her account. Most
                cases come back low risk — Priya's KYC screening is clear, the documents for Robert's
                late mother's death benefit are genuine, and Tom's hardship documents check out — so they
                move on without extra friction.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    </div>

    <div class="agent-tab-panel" data-panel="try" role="tabpanel">
    <section class="panel fc-panel" style="--accent: #ef4444">
        <h2>Try it out — Financial crime review</h2>
        <p class="muted fc-help">
            Pick a Member Case, review its account activity, scan the documents on the case, then
            engage Felix's agent for an explainable risk score and recommended controls. The demo runs
            live against the <code>/fincrime/*</code> endpoints in this app — without Foundry or
            Content Understanding configured, a deterministic assessment built from the case data keeps
            every step working.
        </p>

        <!-- Step 1 — pick a case -->
        <div class="fc-step" data-step="1">
            <div class="fc-step-head">
                <span class="fc-step-num">1</span>
                <h3>Pick a case to review</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="muted">
                The list shows the five scenario cases plus any opened live in the
                <a href="/agents/onboarding">Onboarding</a> Try it out tab.
            </p>
            <div class="fc-case-row">
                <select id="fc-case-select" class="fc-select" aria-label="Member Case">
                    <option value="">— Loading cases… —</option>
                </select>
                <button type="button" id="fc-refresh-btn" class="fc-secondary" title="Reload cases" aria-label="Reload cases">↻</button>
            </div>
            <div class="fc-empty" id="fc-empty" hidden>
                No cases found in memory. Open one from the
                <a href="/agents/onboarding">Onboarding</a> Try it out tab first.
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 2 — review the case and its account activity -->
        <div class="fc-step" data-step="2" id="fc-case-step" hidden>
            <div class="fc-step-head">
                <span class="fc-step-num">2</span>
                <h3>Review the case and its account activity</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="muted">
                The request, the people on the case, the account-activity timeline and the screening
                results Felix's agent will weigh.
            </p>
            <div class="fc-case-grid" id="fc-case-details"></div>

            <div class="fc-review-grid">
                <div class="fc-review-block fc-review-wide">
                    <div class="fc-label">Account-activity timeline</div>
                    <ol class="fc-timeline" id="fc-timeline"><li class="fc-muted-item">Loading…</li></ol>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-review-block">
                    <div class="fc-label">Screening &amp; verification</div>
                    <ul class="fc-screening" id="fc-screening"><li class="fc-muted-item">Loading…</li></ul>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-review-block">
                    <div class="fc-label">People on the case</div>
                    <div id="fc-parties" class="fc-parties"><span class="fc-muted-item">Loading…</span></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 3 — scan the documents on the case -->
        <div class="fc-step" data-step="3" id="fc-docs-step" hidden>
            <div class="fc-step-head">
                <span class="fc-step-num">3</span>
                <h3>Scan the documents on the case</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="muted">
                Each selected document goes through Azure Content Understanding and a deterministic
                checks layer — name and date of birth against the record on file, dates, tamper
                indicators, security features, MRZ check digits, DVS, account age, SMSF registration and
                SVS — and is scored <em>legit</em>, <em>suspicious</em> or <em>fake</em>. Untick a document
                to leave it out, or add a specimen from the popover.
            </p>
            <div class="fc-docs-row">
                <div id="fc-case-docs" class="fc-doc-grid">
                    <div class="fc-doc-empty muted">Loading case documents…</div>
                </div>
                <span id="fc-sample-host"></span>
            </div>
            <button id="fc-scan-btn" class="fc-primary" type="button">Scan documents</button>
            <div id="fc-scan-status" class="fc-status" hidden></div>

            <div id="fc-doc-output" class="fc-doc-output" hidden>
                <div class="fc-label">Document authenticity</div>
                <p class="muted fc-doc-output-hint" id="fc-doc-output-hint"></p>
                <div id="fc-doc-cards" class="fc-doc-cards"></div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 4 — engage the agent -->
        <div class="fc-step" data-step="4" id="fc-process-step" hidden>
            <div class="fc-step-head">
                <span class="fc-step-num">4</span>
                <h3>Engage the Financial Crime Agent</h3>
            </div>
            <p class="muted">
                Felix's agent receives the case, the account-activity timeline, the screening results and
                the document findings, then produces an explainable risk score and recommended controls
                for the human investigator.
            </p>
            <button id="fc-process-btn" class="fc-primary" type="button">Run financial crime review</button>
            <div id="fc-process-status" class="fc-status" hidden></div>

            <div class="engage-tabs-scope" data-engage-role="financial-crime">
                <div class="engage-tabs" role="tablist">
                    <button type="button" class="engage-tab-btn active" data-engage-tab="narrative">Agent Narrative</button>
                    <button type="button" class="engage-tab-btn" data-engage-tab="reference">Reference</button>
                    <button type="button" class="engage-tab-btn" data-engage-tab="prompt">Agent Prompt &amp; Tools</button>
                    <button type="button" class="engage-tab-btn" data-engage-tab="input">Agent Input</button>
                    <button type="button" class="engage-tab-btn" data-engage-tab="output">Raw Output</button>
                </div>

                <div class="engage-tab-panel active" data-engage-tab="narrative">
                    <div class="engage-info-block">
                        <h4>Agent narrative (streamed)</h4>
                        <div class="agent-md engage-narrative-body"><div class="engage-empty">Engage the agent to see the streamed narrative.</div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="engage-tab-panel" data-engage-tab="reference">
                    <div class="engage-info-block">
                        <h4>Reference documents cited by the agent</h4>
                        <div class="engage-references-body"><div class="engage-empty">Engage the agent to see the reference documents cited in its response.</div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="engage-tab-panel" data-engage-tab="prompt">
                    <div class="engage-info-block">
                        <h4>Agent metadata</h4>
                        <div class="engage-info-meta engage-meta"></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="engage-info-block">
                        <h4>System prompt</h4>
                        <pre class="engage-pre engage-prompt-body">Loading…</pre>
                    </div>
                    <div class="engage-info-block">
                        <h4>Tools available</h4>
                        <ul class="engage-tools-list"><li class="engage-empty">Loading…</li></ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="engage-tab-panel" data-engage-tab="input">
                    <div class="engage-info-block">
                        <h4>Prompt sent to the agent</h4>
                        <pre class="engage-pre engage-input-body engage-empty">Engage the agent to capture the input that was sent.</pre>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="engage-tab-panel" data-engage-tab="output">
                    <div class="engage-info-block">
                        <h4>Raw agent output (text, citations, every output item including tool / function calls)</h4>
                        <div class="json-viewer engage-output-body"><div class="engage-empty">Engage the agent to see the full raw response.</div></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step 5 — risk summary & recommended actions -->
        <div class="fc-step" data-step="5" id="fc-output-step" hidden>
            <div class="fc-step-head">
                <span class="fc-step-num">5</span>
                <h3>Risk summary &amp; recommended actions</h3>
            </div>

            <div class="fc-risk-card">
                <div class="fc-risk-head">
                    <span class="fc-risk-label">Financial crime risk</span>
                    <span class="fc-risk-pill" id="fc-risk-pill"></span>
                    <span class="fc-risk-num" id="fc-risk-num"></span>
                </div>
                <p id="fc-risk-summary" class="fc-risk-summary"></p>
                <p id="fc-agent-view" class="fc-agent-view" hidden></p>
            </div>

            <div class="fc-output-grid">
                <div class="fc-output-block fc-output-wide">
                    <div class="fc-label">Risk indicators &amp; evidence</div>
                    <ul id="fc-indicators" class="fc-indicators"></ul>
                    <p id="fc-score-breakdown" class="fc-score-breakdown"></p>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-output-block">
                    <div class="fc-label">Recommended actions</div>
                    <ol id="fc-actions" class="fc-actions"></ol>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-output-block">
                    <div class="fc-label">What checked out</div>
                    <ul id="fc-clear" class="fc-clear"></ul>
                </div>
                <div class="fc-output-block fc-output-wide">
                    <div class="fc-label">Human approval required</div>
                    <p id="fc-approval" class="fc-approval-text"></p>
                    <p id="fc-smr" class="fc-smr" hidden></p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    .fc-panel { --fc-accent: #ef4444; }
    .fc-help { margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
    .fc-panel code { background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.12); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.85rem; }

    .fc-step {
        border: 1px solid rgba(120, 150, 200, 0.18);
        background: rgba(15, 22, 38, 0.4);
        border-radius: 12px;
        padding: 0.95rem 1.1rem 1rem 1.1rem;
        margin-top: 0.9rem;
    }
    .fc-step-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
    .fc-step-head h3 { margin: 0; color: #fff; font-size: 1rem; }
    .fc-step-num {
        display: inline-grid; place-items: center;
        width: 1.55rem; height: 1.55rem;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fc-accent) 22%, rgba(20, 28, 46, 0.7));
        border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--fc-accent) 55%, transparent);
        color: var(--fc-accent);
        font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700;
    }
    .fc-step .muted { color: var(--cw-muted, #97a3b6); font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0.35rem 0 0.7rem 0; }
    .fc-label {
        font-size: 0.66rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
        color: var(--cw-muted, #97a3b6); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    }
    .fc-muted-item { color: var(--cw-muted, #97a3b6); font-size: 0.84rem; list-style: none; }

    /* Step 1 */
    .fc-case-row { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; align-items: center; }
    .fc-select {
        flex: 1;
        background: rgba(10, 16, 28, 0.7);
        border: 1px solid rgba(120, 150, 200, 0.22);
        border-radius: 6px;
        color: #fff;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;
    }
    .fc-select:focus {
        outline: none;
        border-color: var(--fc-accent);
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb, var(--fc-accent) 25%, transparent);
    }
    .fc-secondary {
        background: transparent;
        color: rgba(238, 242, 247, 0.86);
        border: 1px solid rgba(120, 150, 200, 0.32);
        border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        cursor: pointer;
    }
    .fc-secondary:hover { background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05); color: #fff; }
    .fc-empty {
        margin-top: 0.6rem;
        padding: 0.6rem 0.8rem;
        background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.10);
        border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35);
        border-radius: 8px;
        color: #fcd34d;
        font-size: 0.86rem;
    }
    .fc-empty a { color: #fde68a; }

    /* Step 2 */
    .fc-case-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 0.45rem 0.85rem;
        font-size: 0.86rem;
        color: rgba(238, 242, 247, 0.86);
    }
    .fc-case-grid .k {
        display: inline-block; min-width: 118px;
        color: var(--cw-muted, #97a3b6); font-weight: 600;
        text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.66rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        margin-right: 0.5rem;
    }
    .fc-case-grid .span-2 { grid-column: span 2; }
    .fc-review-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 0.7rem;
        margin-top: 0.85rem;
    }
    .fc-review-block, .fc-output-block {
        background: rgba(10, 16, 28, 0.7);
        border: 1px solid rgba(120, 150, 200, 0.18);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 0.65rem 0.85rem;
    }
    .fc-review-wide, .fc-output-wide { grid-column: span 2; }
    @@media (max-width: 820px) {
        .fc-case-grid, .fc-review-grid, .fc-output-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        .fc-case-grid .span-2, .fc-review-wide, .fc-output-wide { grid-column: span 1; }
    }

    .fc-timeline { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    .fc-timeline li {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 172px 1fr;
        gap: 0.7rem;
        padding: 0.45rem 0 0.45rem 0.7rem;
        border-left: 3px solid #94a3b8;
        margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    }
    .fc-timeline li.flag-red { border-left-color: #ef4444; }
    .fc-timeline li.flag-amber { border-left-color: #f59e0b; }
    .fc-timeline li.flag-ok { border-left-color: #22c55e; }
    .fc-timeline li.flag-info { border-left-color: #64748b; }
    .fc-tl-when {
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
        font-size: 0.78rem; color: rgba(238, 242, 247, 0.78);
    }
    .fc-tl-channel {
        font-size: 0.64rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em;
        color: var(--cw-muted, #97a3b6); font-weight: 700;
    }
    .fc-tl-summary { color: #fff; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.88rem; }
    .fc-tl-detail { color: rgba(238, 242, 247, 0.8); font-size: 0.83rem; line-height: 1.45; }
    @@media (max-width: 720px) { .fc-timeline li { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.2rem; } }

    .fc-screening, .fc-clear { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.45; color: rgba(238, 242, 247, 0.88); }
    .fc-screening li, .fc-clear li { display: flex; gap: 0.45rem; align-items: flex-start; padding: 0.18rem 0; }
    .fc-icon { width: 1rem; flex: 0 0 1rem; font-weight: 700; }
    .fc-icon.pass { color: #86efac; }
    .fc-icon.fail { color: #fca5a5; }
    .fc-icon.warn { color: #fcd34d; }
    .fc-icon.info, .fc-icon.na { color: #94a3b8; }
    .fc-screening .fc-check-name { font-weight: 600; color: rgba(238, 242, 247, 0.94); }

    .fc-parties { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem; }
    .fc-party {
        background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.08);
        border: 1px solid rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.28);
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 0.2rem 0.65rem;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        color: rgba(238, 242, 247, 0.92);
    }
    .fc-party small { color: var(--cw-muted, #97a3b6); }
    .fc-trusted { margin: 0.6rem 0 0 0; font-size: 0.82rem; color: rgba(238, 242, 247, 0.86); }
    .fc-trusted strong { color: #86efac; }

    /* Buttons & status */
    .fc-primary {
        background: var(--fc-accent);
        color: #2a0606;
        border: none;
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 0.55rem 1.1rem;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        cursor: pointer;
        margin-top: 0.6rem;
    }
    .fc-primary:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed; }
    .fc-status { margin-top: 0.6rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: rgba(238, 242, 247, 0.88); }
    .fc-status.error { color: #fca5a5; }
    .fc-status .spinner {
        display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 12px;
        border: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3); border-top-color: #fff;
        border-radius: 50%; margin-right: 6px; vertical-align: middle;
        animation: fc-spin 0.7s linear infinite;
    }
    @@keyframes fc-spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }

    /* Step 3 — case documents */
    .fc-docs-row { display: flex; gap: 0.7rem; align-items: flex-start; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .fc-doc-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(175px, 1fr));
        gap: 0.55rem;
        flex: 1;
        min-width: 260px;
    }
    .fc-doc-empty { padding: 0.55rem; }
    .fc-doc-tile {
        position: relative;
        background: rgba(10, 16, 28, 0.7);
        border: 1px solid rgba(120, 150, 200, 0.22);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 0.55rem;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.35rem;
    }
    .fc-doc-tile.selected {
        border-color: var(--fc-accent);
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--fc-accent) 40%, transparent);
    }
    .fc-doc-tile img {
        width: 100%; height: 100px; object-fit: cover;
        border-radius: 5px; background: #0a101c; cursor: zoom-in;
    }
    .fc-doc-title { font-size: 0.78rem; color: rgba(238, 242, 247, 0.92); line-height: 1.25; }
